  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A deep-tunnel fire-mine situated three leagues below Nightfall Shelf's main warren, accessible only through merchant-controlled routes. Locally called **the Scar-mouth**. The volcanic vein feeding ☽'shadow Samsiavae~ runs hotter than any other known fire-core deposit on The Berg — ambient temperature holds at a reported 15.4 degrees, sufficient to raise ice-blisters on exposed skin within the hour. Work shifts are kept short by necessity.
    
    The mine was established during the Faction Wars and passed through several hands violently. The Midnight Claws, the criminal syndicate that once dominated Nightfall Shelf's shadow economy, held the site for an extended period, carving bioluminescent insignia into the eastern cavern wall. Those claw-marks still glow, though they thin visibly each season. Control was lost — the archive does not record whether by force, negotiation, or the corruption that eventually overtook the deeper workings.
    
    ## Corruption and Cleansing
    
    Corruption spread through the mine from a breach associated with the ability known as Shawl☽ Sun. Miners died. Their names are not spoken above ground, though small offerings of rendered seal-fat are left at the deepest brazier in their memory. Augur ☽'Milucaum~ Shadow-bane conducted the cleansing, leaving long scorch-trails across the cavern walls — the ice beneath remains brittle and discolored, scarring that will outlast any current tenant. The Aureate merchant guild now operates the mine, working around the Midnight Claws' fading insignia without troubling to remove it.
    
    Fire-cores lost during the collapse of the lower workings still radiate heat from the sealed rubble, warm and unreachable, sinking deeper into strata no crew has excavated.
    
    ## The Scar-Mouth Song and the Mist~Record
    
    The mine's layered history — criminal tenure, corruption, cleansing — has been encoded into the **Scar-Mouth Song**, a Nightshelf work-chant sung in fragments by fire-tenders on deep shifts. The complete verse has not been assembled since the mystic ☽'voidae vanished. The refrain is considered unlucky to sing above mid-depth.
    
    The artifact known as ☽'somunis' Mist~Record, a warm tome of bioluminescent text predating penguin civilization, is stored at this site. Its keepers have fared poorly. The mine holds what it holds.
