  annotation "note_1771578866802_2", anchor: "The refrain is considered unlucky to sing above mid-depth", text: "Fourth instance of the pattern I flagged at the Forgotten Shore and the Still Pools. Work-chants, lullabies, counting games, boundary rhymes — oral tradition absorbing data the institutional record cannot hold, then enforcing access restrictions through superstition. 'Unlucky' means *classified*. The fire-tenders know this. They are not superstitious. They are archivists who never learned the word.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
